// sexp module: S-expression reader (tavm bridge, test/backend).
//
// C implementation: lib/sexp.c (lazily dlopen'd on first sexp.* call).
// sexp.parse returns the LIST OF TOP-LEVEL FORMS — a heterogeneous tree of
// pairs/symbols/ints/strings/nil/true/false, so the return is deliberately
// unannotated here: a concrete annotation would be a lie (empty input is
// nil, an error is -1, success is a pair chain). The runtime is the
// contract, same doctrine as lib/math.ta:
//
//   sexp.parse(text) -> nil-terminated list of top-level forms
//                       (list-of-forms: one form -> ((form)));
//                       -1 on a hard error, details via sexp.err()
//   sexp.err()       -> string describing the last parse error, "" if the
//                       previous sexp.parse succeeded
//
// Grammar v1: ';' line comments, '(...) lists, 'x -> (quote x), int48,
// symbols, strings with \\ \" \n \t \r escapes, ()/nil -> nil,
// true/false. Nesting depth <= 10000.
//
// A '.' in element position is the pair tail, not an element: (a . b) is
// the dotted pair (a . b), (a . (b c)) is the plain list (a b c). lower
// 产物里就有这种形态：match/receive 的模式是点对 ((pair . rest) 是
// car=pair / cdr=rest 的点对)，所以 .kl writer 必须能写出、reader 必须
// 能读回（详见 lib/bootstrap/kl.ta 与 docs/kl-format.md）。首元素位置的
// '.'（前面没有元素）仍是普通符号 —— writer 能写出的 `.` 头列表要读得回。
//
// `'` reads a NAME: after an atom token it interns the token text as a
// symbol rather than the value it spells ('nil is the symbol nil, '42 the
// symbol 42) — same rule as the TA parser, and what lets the .kl writer
// emit every symbol as 'NAME. A list/string after `'` still reads
// recursively: '(a b) -> (quote (a b)), '"s" -> (quote "s").

external fn sexp.parse(text)
external fn sexp.err() -> String
